I need a small daily ETL job. Our weather stations have a REST API that returns JSON with pagination. I want to pull yesterday's readings, flatten them, do some basic cleaning and upsert into a SQLite db, so if I run it twice for the same day I don't get duplicates. It will run from cron at 3am. The API key is in an env var WEATHER_API_KEY.

Example response from GET https://api.wetternetz.example/v2/observations?from=...&to=...&limit=500:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "station": {"id": "WS-014", "name": "Hafen Nord", "elevation_m": 4},
      "observed_at": "2026-10-20T00:10:00+02:00",
      "measurements": {
        "temp_c": 9.4,
        "humidity_pct": 88,
        "wind": {"speed_ms": 6.1, "dir_deg": 250},
        "rain_mm": 0.0
      },
      "qc_flags": []
    }
  ],
  "next_cursor": "eyJvZmZzZXQiOjUwMH0="
}
```

next_cursor is null on the last page, and you pass it back as ?cursor=. Sometimes a station has no wind sensor, then "wind" is missing completely. Sensors sometimes report garbage like temp_c = -999 or humidity 140.
